WEBVTT

00:17.220 --> 00:19.220
What a refreshing breeze...

00:19.350 --> 00:24.520
Don't you think sunny days smell great?
Big brother?

00:24.600 --> 00:25.890
Oh, I see.

00:26.100 --> 00:29.860
That pleasant smell is from the sun.

00:30.070 --> 00:32.150
I was sure it was you.

00:32.240 --> 00:34.650
Oh, big brother!

00:36.610 --> 00:39.740
It's just like the grounds of Aries Palace.

00:39.830 --> 00:40.780
Yeah.

00:42.120 --> 00:43.750
Big brother.

00:43.910 --> 00:46.790
Can I ask you to do me a favor?

00:46.920 --> 00:49.290
A favor? Ask and see.

00:49.540 --> 00:52.590
I want to hear a story.

00:52.670 --> 00:53.880
Hear a story?

00:53.970 --> 00:54.880
Yes.

00:55.090 --> 01:00.140
Like the ones you used to tell me in those grounds
when we were young.

01:00.430 --> 01:01.470
Nunnally...

01:02.100 --> 01:06.140
That was in the time when we were still happy.

01:06.730 --> 01:11.820
I remember it well. Your innocent eyes
as you begged me to tell you a story.

01:11.940 --> 01:16.740
And your excited, sparkling smile
as I told you my trifling stories.

01:17.280 --> 01:21.740
If you tell me I could see
that dear smile once again,

01:22.080 --> 01:26.290
I'd do everything in my power to grant your wish.

01:26.460 --> 01:31.290
At least it should soothe your battered heart,
if only for a little while...

01:31.500 --> 01:33.500
Lelouch vi Britannia commands!

01:33.630 --> 01:38.430
The characters of Code Geass
to appear in the story I narrate and

01:38.510 --> 01:41.640
entertain my beloved sister, Nunnally!

01:44.890 --> 01:46.890
What? What's this?

01:46.980 --> 01:48.440
What's happened...

01:48.520 --> 01:50.060
My eyes suddenly...

01:50.310 --> 01:53.690
Bibbity, bobbity, bobbity, boo.

01:53.860 --> 01:57.490
Bibbity, bobbity, records are memories...

01:57.570 --> 01:59.860
Oh! A cute rabbit!

01:59.990 --> 02:01.660
All white and fluffy!

02:01.780 --> 02:05.040
Hey, take a look, big brother. How strange!

02:05.250 --> 02:08.960
The rabbit is taking photos
with its mobile phone...

02:09.830 --> 02:12.250
The rabbit is taking photos
with its mobile phone!

02:12.340 --> 02:13.170
Weird!

02:13.290 --> 02:15.460
People's memories are fuzzy.

02:15.550 --> 02:17.340
Bibbity, bobbity,

02:17.470 --> 02:20.340
so records are memories, bibbity...

02:20.430 --> 02:21.840
Wait a minute, White Rabbit!

02:21.930 --> 02:24.300
Why do you have something
like a mobile phone? You--

02:37.780 --> 02:38.820
And just like that,

02:39.030 --> 02:42.200
the opening act of
the girl's adventurous journey began.

02:43.030 --> 02:46.410
Chasing after the mysterious white rabbit,
she fell into a deep hole,

02:46.540 --> 02:51.870
that went deeper and deeper,
and just as she started to worry that

02:52.000 --> 02:56.880
it might go all the way
to the other side of this planet,

02:57.090 --> 03:01.550
she finally landed softly at the bottom.

03:02.050 --> 03:05.180
There was no sign of the White Rabbit.

03:05.310 --> 03:08.560
Instead, there was a small door...

03:08.640 --> 03:12.690
Could the White Rabbit be
on the other side of this door?

03:12.770 --> 03:16.400
The girl thought,
and she tried to go through too,

03:16.520 --> 03:19.320
but it was much too small for her
to pass through.

03:19.440 --> 03:24.820
She was troubled and looked around
to find a table nearby with a small bottle on it.

03:25.200 --> 03:28.740
There was something written on the bottle.

03:28.910 --> 03:30.750
"Drink me"?

03:30.870 --> 03:33.080
I should drink this?

03:35.630 --> 03:36.840
Aaah.

03:37.880 --> 03:39.840
What? Aaaaah...

03:40.170 --> 03:43.380
The girl's body started shrinking
before her very eyes and

03:43.470 --> 03:46.350
in an instant she was pocket size.

03:46.970 --> 03:48.100
Oh,

03:48.350 --> 03:52.940
if only I could really put you
in my pocket and protect you,

03:53.100 --> 03:57.940
I wouldn't have gone to all that trouble and got
the whole world involved in that overblown thing...

03:59.730 --> 04:02.070
Despite shrinking the girl was still lovely and

04:02.150 --> 04:05.110
she was pleased
she could now fit through the door.

04:05.200 --> 04:06.370
However...

04:06.450 --> 04:08.280
Oh, no! The key...

04:08.530 --> 04:12.790
A golden key was visible on the nearby table.

04:12.910 --> 04:16.790
But it was out of the shrunken girl's reach.

04:16.880 --> 04:18.380
What can I do?

04:18.460 --> 04:23.670
Then she saw a plate
under the table with a cake on it.

04:24.090 --> 04:25.970
Another message was written on it.

04:26.090 --> 04:27.800
"Eat me"?

04:27.930 --> 04:29.390
I wonder!

04:29.470 --> 04:30.350
Eh!

04:31.640 --> 04:33.350
Ah, aaaaah!

04:33.690 --> 04:35.480
It was just as she'd suspected.

04:35.600 --> 04:38.360
The clever girl got bigger and bigger and

04:38.480 --> 04:42.480
finally she could reach the key on the table.

04:42.570 --> 04:44.190
However...

04:44.320 --> 04:47.820
Oh no, now I can't fit through the door again.

04:47.950 --> 04:51.870
Really! Silly me, what am I playing at?

04:52.160 --> 04:57.170
The sweet and pure girl became sad
and started to cry.

04:57.500 --> 05:02.880
Thereupon something strange happened.
In an instant her tears pooled up around her and

05:03.050 --> 05:09.180
before you knew it
she was floating gently in a lake of her own tears.

05:09.600 --> 05:12.470
She tried desperately to head towards the shore.

05:12.560 --> 05:13.850
What should I do?

05:13.930 --> 05:18.770
I'm soaked through, I'm in no state to be going
anywhere, never mind chasing after the White Rabbit...

05:19.110 --> 05:20.690
You poor thing, Nunnally...

05:20.770 --> 05:24.150
Don't worry,
I'll soon dry those soaking clothes for you!

05:25.110 --> 05:28.160
She reached the shore but was at a loss,

05:28.700 --> 05:32.870
when she realized
a Dodo had appeared unnoticed.

05:33.080 --> 05:34.160
Hello.

05:38.000 --> 05:41.540
The Dodo courteously returned the greeting
and with few words,

05:41.670 --> 05:43.710
first led the girl to the bathroom.

05:43.800 --> 05:47.550
As the girl warmed herself up,
her clothes were cleaned, dried and

05:47.680 --> 05:49.510
ironed with just the right amount of starch and

05:49.590 --> 05:52.800
just as she came out,
there was a prepared fruit drink waiting for her.

05:52.890 --> 05:55.350
Her hair was done as she was dressed and

05:55.430 --> 05:58.600
in no time at all, cute Nunnally was
back to her usual self.

05:58.730 --> 06:00.440
Th-Thank you.

06:00.730 --> 06:03.070
Good job as always, Sayoko.

06:03.520 --> 06:07.940
To commemorate their meeting
the girl took a photo of the Dodo,

06:08.450 --> 06:11.950
as a camera had slipped
unnoticed into her hand.

06:12.490 --> 06:15.450
However, after the Dodo left,

06:15.580 --> 06:19.830
when she examined closely what she thought was
a camera, she found it was actually a mobile phone.

06:19.920 --> 06:22.920
The White Rabbit must have dropped
this on her way.

06:23.000 --> 06:25.380
I must hurry and deliver it to her.

06:25.460 --> 06:30.220
The girl set off walking into the forest
behind the shore to search for the White Rabbit.

06:30.430 --> 06:34.680
But she had no idea where on earth
she should go to find the Rabbit.

06:34.760 --> 06:37.430
As she wondered along in her bewildered state,

06:37.560 --> 06:41.440
she met a large Caterpillar smoking a hookah.

06:41.520 --> 06:43.270
Hello, Ms. Caterpillar.

06:43.360 --> 06:46.610
Well, may I ask you a question?

06:46.690 --> 06:49.280
The girl asked and as luck would have it,

06:49.400 --> 06:52.450
the Caterpillar knew where
the White Rabbit's house was.

06:52.740 --> 06:55.950
After being told the directions,
she politely thanked the Caterpillar and

06:56.080 --> 06:58.750
then hurriedly set off towards the house.

06:59.250 --> 07:02.750
But for some reason,
the Caterpillar halted her progress.

07:02.960 --> 07:04.960
Is something wrong?

07:05.040 --> 07:09.800
The Caterpillar told her that the bottled medicine
that made her smaller and

07:09.920 --> 07:12.430
the cake that made her bigger were her inventions.

07:12.510 --> 07:15.470
Huh? My impressions on having used them?

07:15.560 --> 07:17.810
Um, well...

07:17.890 --> 07:19.560
As she obediently answered,

07:19.640 --> 07:23.480
the Caterpillar asked more and more questions
while puffing away on her hookah.

07:23.600 --> 07:26.150
Her opinions were sought on the color, taste,
smell, how it felt going down,

07:26.270 --> 07:29.230
how long it took for the effect to appear,
any feelings of side effects,

07:29.320 --> 07:31.780
and any thoughts on how they could be improved...

07:31.900 --> 07:33.740
Um, well, ah...

07:33.820 --> 07:37.030
Hey, no-one cares about your hobby, Rakshata!

07:37.490 --> 07:39.490
The girl finally left the Caterpillar and

07:39.620 --> 07:43.920
following the given directions,
she headed further into the forest.

07:44.330 --> 07:46.500
Just as she was wondering
how long she had walked for and

07:46.630 --> 07:49.340
was thinking about having a rest,

07:50.130 --> 07:53.180
suddenly the thicket of trees
seemed to open up

07:53.300 --> 07:58.050
before her to reveal a lovely house.

07:58.470 --> 08:01.600
Right, you lot better do your utmost
to be hospitable to Nunnally and

08:01.680 --> 08:04.560
soothe her troubled heart
until she is totally content!

08:04.770 --> 08:05.940
Excuse me.

08:06.020 --> 08:08.980
Isn't this the White Rabbit's house?

08:12.240 --> 08:13.110
Who are you?

08:13.200 --> 08:18.450
My name is Nunnally and
I'm lost in this Wonderland.

08:18.740 --> 08:20.160
What do you want?

08:20.240 --> 08:25.420
Um, this phone isn't yours
by any chance, is it?

08:25.540 --> 08:27.880
Ah, thanks.

08:28.090 --> 08:29.090
Oh, good,

08:29.210 --> 08:30.880
here you are.

08:34.760 --> 08:36.510
I don't know this memory.

08:36.590 --> 08:38.140
Oh, I'm sorry.

08:38.220 --> 08:39.720
I took that...

08:39.850 --> 08:41.890
Come in.
I want to thank you.

08:41.970 --> 08:43.890
There's no need for thanks...

08:44.020 --> 08:47.560
No need to be polite,
the Duchess has just dropped by as well.

08:47.690 --> 08:48.900
The Duchess?

08:48.980 --> 08:49.900
Please.

08:50.020 --> 08:52.650
Well, okay then.

08:52.780 --> 08:54.950
The Wonderland Broken Hearts Contest.

08:55.070 --> 08:57.280
The Wonderland Bravest Declaration of Love Test.

08:57.410 --> 08:59.740
The Wonderland Couple Swapping Battle.

08:59.830 --> 09:01.660
The Wonder, the...

09:01.950 --> 09:02.910
Duchess.

09:03.040 --> 09:04.500
Oh my, a guest?

09:04.580 --> 09:05.290
This is Nunnally.

09:05.620 --> 09:07.580
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

09:07.710 --> 09:10.710
She returned my lost memories.

09:10.800 --> 09:13.050
Right, it's decided then.

09:13.130 --> 09:16.300
Today's event is
the Wonderland Nunnally Appreciation Day!

09:16.430 --> 09:16.970
Eh?

09:17.090 --> 09:18.430
Look forward to it.

09:18.510 --> 09:23.270
My cook is making a splendid feast for it now!

09:24.270 --> 09:26.020
Sorry to have kept you waiting!

09:26.310 --> 09:28.270
It's here, it's here!

09:28.850 --> 09:30.690
Um, that's unusual food...

09:30.770 --> 09:31.900
What is it?

09:32.020 --> 09:35.530
Sweet and sour F.L.E.I.J.A.,
garlic sauté F.L.E.I.J.A. and

09:35.610 --> 09:37.780
Mediterranean style seafood F.L.E.I.J.A.

09:37.910 --> 09:40.490
Just because it sounds like paella but...

09:40.620 --> 09:42.030
Is the taste okay?

09:42.370 --> 09:44.200
It's more than okay, it's very powerful,

09:44.290 --> 09:45.540
it's F.L.E.I.J.A...

09:45.620 --> 09:48.540
I'm not sure I liked the way she said that...

09:48.790 --> 09:51.290
Sorry, but can you make something else--

09:51.420 --> 09:52.960
Duchess, you always do this!

09:53.090 --> 09:55.130
"Make anything you like," you say,

09:55.210 --> 09:57.170
but when I do you complain about it!

09:57.300 --> 10:01.970
Well, if you made proper food
instead of a tactical weapon, I wouldn't moan.

10:02.050 --> 10:03.510
It's not a tactical weapon!

10:03.640 --> 10:04.810
It's a strategic weapon.

10:04.970 --> 10:07.270
So you admit it's not food, right?

10:08.480 --> 10:11.690
Excuse me!
I'm the March Hare who lives next door!

10:11.810 --> 10:14.690
Is there someone here who occasionally
screams hysterically?

10:14.820 --> 10:15.650
No, there's not!

10:15.740 --> 10:17.070
Yes, it's you.

10:17.150 --> 10:20.240
We can hear you in the forest,
and we can't have a relaxing tea party.

10:20.320 --> 10:21.360
Isn't that right, Dormouse?!

10:21.490 --> 10:22.820
Zzz...

10:22.950 --> 10:24.160
Mr. Dormouse?

10:24.450 --> 10:26.330
Don't mind him, leave him be.

10:26.450 --> 10:30.710
March Hare, I'm sorry
about my cook disturbing you.

10:30.830 --> 10:32.460
I'll have a word with her later...

10:32.540 --> 10:34.170
Duchess, you're always talking
like you're above me!

10:34.340 --> 10:36.050
That's the noise I'm talking about.

10:37.010 --> 10:38.010
It's redundant.

10:38.090 --> 10:38.880
Huh?

10:39.380 --> 10:40.680
Having two rabbits.

10:41.050 --> 10:42.010
That's true.

10:42.640 --> 10:45.510
This forest only needs one cute mascot.

10:45.600 --> 10:48.560
Really? Then why don't you become a giraffe?

10:48.680 --> 10:50.640
I think you'd be better as a hippo.

10:50.810 --> 10:52.400
Um, ah...

10:52.520 --> 10:53.730
Hm.

10:53.860 --> 10:55.940
We'll let's settle it.

10:56.030 --> 10:59.030
Here and now...who is the strongest rabbit.

10:59.150 --> 11:00.740
Eh? Strongest?

11:00.860 --> 11:03.410
Right...my Guren Type-02...

11:03.950 --> 11:06.330
Or my Mordred...which one...

11:06.410 --> 11:08.040
W-Wait a minute, both of you!

11:08.370 --> 11:10.500
Haaaaah!

11:13.380 --> 11:14.920
Oh no, Duchess!

11:15.040 --> 11:15.920
We have to stop them!

11:16.050 --> 11:19.550
At last it's started,
the Wonderland Rabbit Championship!

11:19.670 --> 11:23.010
Who will claim the rabbit mascot crown,
White or March?

11:23.090 --> 11:25.600
Um, ah? Mr. Dormouse, stop them!

11:25.720 --> 11:30.060
Duchess! Surely today
you're going to accept my love, right?

11:30.560 --> 11:32.310
Um, ah, Cook!

11:34.900 --> 11:39.030
It seems I'm in the way,
so I think I'll be on my way!

11:39.110 --> 11:40.820
See you later.

11:41.030 --> 11:42.900
Stop, stop!

11:42.990 --> 11:46.240
Is this what this story is supposed to be about?

11:46.330 --> 11:47.990
Now that you mention it...

11:48.080 --> 11:49.740
And what's more, he's not even here.

11:49.830 --> 11:50.750
That's true.

11:50.830 --> 11:54.750
Right, when you have all of us,
the Dormouse, the March Hare, who springs to mind...

11:54.830 --> 11:56.170
The Mad Hatter!

11:58.250 --> 12:03.130
Well, at least I was able to return
the phone to the White Rabbit.

12:03.260 --> 12:04.090
It's about time...

12:04.590 --> 12:08.220
Ah! Um, oh no!

12:08.310 --> 12:09.220
What's wrong?

12:13.850 --> 12:15.100
Ah, yes.

12:15.190 --> 12:20.280
Actually I'm not sure
how to get back to the world I came from.

12:20.400 --> 12:21.440
I see.

12:21.530 --> 12:24.780
You've lost your way home.

12:24.860 --> 12:28.160
As a matter of fact, I think I've lost something too.

12:28.280 --> 12:30.370
Your way home, Fawn?

12:30.790 --> 12:31.790
No.

12:31.870 --> 12:33.620
Just everything that's important.

12:33.750 --> 12:34.710
What?

12:34.960 --> 12:38.170
But, I think I shouldn't try to get it back.

12:38.420 --> 12:41.000
Because I've got a feeling that if I remember it,

12:41.130 --> 12:44.220
it will break into tiny pieces and

12:44.300 --> 12:45.880
be scattered away.

12:45.970 --> 12:47.340
Fawn...

12:47.680 --> 12:49.800
And with those deep words,

12:49.890 --> 12:52.270
the Fawn went on her way.

12:52.770 --> 12:58.270
I was really hoping you'd tell her the way home,
Shirley, not a poem...

12:58.360 --> 12:59.900
And as for those others before,

12:59.980 --> 13:04.820
where was the hospitality that was meant to
soothe Nunnally's heart?! Unbelievable!

13:05.320 --> 13:08.700
Having no clue how to return to her world,

13:08.820 --> 13:12.330
the girl decided there was no choice
but to continue on deeper into the forest.

13:12.790 --> 13:15.830
After walking a while she came across
a road that branched into three.

13:16.210 --> 13:20.590
There she met two twins called
Tweedle Dum and Tweedle Dee.

13:20.670 --> 13:23.340
Even though they didn't look at all alike and

13:23.460 --> 13:27.760
Tweedle Dee looked a whole lot older,

13:27.840 --> 13:31.850
they insisted they were twins
so it must have been so.

13:32.010 --> 13:35.600
Excuse me, may I ask you two something?

13:35.890 --> 13:37.980
When she asked them the way home,

13:38.190 --> 13:41.860
the twins pointed to the roads going left and right.

13:42.110 --> 13:46.490
The twins argued over everything and
couldn't agree on anything.

13:46.780 --> 13:51.120
As they were no help,
she decided to take the road in the middle.

13:51.830 --> 13:53.280
She walked a little while longer,

13:53.370 --> 13:56.750
and before she knew it,
a high wall by the road appeared.

13:57.710 --> 14:02.710
When she looked up,
there was an egg as big as person on it.

14:02.840 --> 14:06.970
Actually it was more like an egg person
than a person sized egg.

14:07.050 --> 14:11.720
That's right, she had met Humpty Dumpty.

14:11.970 --> 14:15.970
However, he didn't know the way
to the girl's home either.

14:16.060 --> 14:17.770
Oh, I see...

14:17.890 --> 14:24.270
Seeing the girl's downhearted and slumped figure,
Humpty Dumpty became sad too,

14:24.400 --> 14:29.740
so in place of the way home, he told her the story
of the man who was transformed into a Jabberwock.

14:30.450 --> 14:33.740
Oh, my son, beware of the Jabberwock!

14:33.910 --> 14:37.790
With his tassels flapping in the wind!
And his twinkling Geass Canceler!

14:38.580 --> 14:42.210
After hearing the legend of the Jabberwock,
the girl felt slightly better and

14:42.290 --> 14:44.420
started walking again.

14:44.550 --> 14:47.010
Why that made her feel better I don't know,

14:47.090 --> 14:49.630
but good job Jeremiah, as always!

14:49.760 --> 14:50.760
However...

14:52.010 --> 14:53.850
Oh, how embarrassing...

14:53.930 --> 14:55.760
Nothing to be embarrassed about,

14:56.100 --> 14:58.430
the sound of your tummy rumbling is

14:58.520 --> 15:03.770
like a magnificent symphony that would even put
an angel's song to shame, Nunnally.

15:04.520 --> 15:08.070
Of course it was not unreasonable that
the girl's tummy was making such a noise.

15:08.320 --> 15:11.740
After all she had not eaten once

15:11.820 --> 15:15.120
since she had found herself
cast astray in this Wonderland.

15:15.490 --> 15:20.160
Furthermore, her best chance had been at the White
Rabbit's house and we know how that went.

15:20.460 --> 15:22.370
Gradually her legs became heavy and

15:22.460 --> 15:25.540
and just as she felt she was going to collapse,

15:25.630 --> 15:30.050
as luck would have it,
she felt someone's gaze upon her.

15:30.130 --> 15:31.130
Hurry up!

15:31.260 --> 15:36.260
You lot better feed her immediately
with the most delicious food she's ever eaten!

15:36.810 --> 15:38.510
Congratulations!

15:38.850 --> 15:39.520
Huh?

15:39.640 --> 15:41.640
You're hungry, right?

15:41.770 --> 15:43.230
Y...Yes.

15:43.310 --> 15:46.360
In that case,
we've got a box lunch for you over here.

15:46.480 --> 15:47.270
What?

15:47.440 --> 15:52.030
Today we've come from our house
on the beach for a picnic.

15:52.280 --> 15:58.990
And this Walrus has made a special lunch for it
which I was really looking forward to eating,

15:59.120 --> 16:05.580
but seeing you about to drop from hunger,
it would be wrong not to share it with you,

16:05.670 --> 16:08.380
even though I really want to eat it all myself.

16:08.500 --> 16:11.460
And yet you seem surprisingly
happy about it, Mr. Carpenter.

16:11.550 --> 16:13.170
Not at all.

16:13.260 --> 16:18.010
This smile just reflects the happiness
I get from being able to help this poor girl out.

16:18.140 --> 16:21.310
Right, hurry up and eat...
no need to be polite,

16:21.390 --> 16:22.930
you can scoff it all up.

16:23.190 --> 16:24.520
Thank you!

16:24.850 --> 16:26.020
Wow!

16:29.020 --> 16:30.190
Excuse me, what's this?

16:30.280 --> 16:31.360
Fried chicken!

16:31.490 --> 16:34.530
I thought just frying it normally would be boring,

16:34.610 --> 16:36.860
so instead of the usual flour and salad oil,

16:36.950 --> 16:40.910
I tried using black sugar and
industrial lubricating oil.

16:41.040 --> 16:42.040
And what's this?

16:42.120 --> 16:43.250
Fried noodles!

16:43.370 --> 16:46.210
I'd always wanted to make my own noodles.

16:46.330 --> 16:49.960
Home made noodles are known for
being refreshing and chewy,

16:50.050 --> 16:53.300
so I thought I'd add some
refreshing and chewy mint gum.

16:53.670 --> 16:55.430
Well...

16:55.970 --> 16:57.300
What's this?

16:57.430 --> 16:58.890
Steak!

16:58.970 --> 17:00.560
What meat?

17:03.640 --> 17:05.060
Please say something!

17:05.190 --> 17:06.480
It's a secret.

17:07.190 --> 17:08.810
Well, it's time I got going...

17:09.060 --> 17:10.980
What?
But you haven't eaten one mouthful...

17:11.070 --> 17:14.740
The kindness you two have shown me is
better than any feast.

17:14.820 --> 17:17.950
My stomach has already become full
with gratitude,

17:18.070 --> 17:21.080
so thanks to both of you! Take care! Bye!

17:21.200 --> 17:22.580
W-Wait a minute!

17:22.660 --> 17:24.250
Isn't that lucky?

17:24.330 --> 17:26.750
What was it you just said, Mr. Carpenter?

17:26.870 --> 17:29.750
That you wanted to eat it all yourself.

17:29.880 --> 17:31.920
No, um, that was...

17:32.050 --> 17:34.920
Actually my best dish is these fried dumplings.

17:35.050 --> 17:38.510
The filling is frog's...no, I'll tell you after,
something for you to look forward to!

17:38.590 --> 17:39.800
Not really...

17:40.100 --> 17:42.600
Let me feed you for once.

17:42.680 --> 17:43.890
Right, don't hold back.

17:43.970 --> 17:45.310
Gyaaah!

17:45.770 --> 17:50.060
It seems the way they cook in this world
is totally different.

17:50.150 --> 17:52.980
I wonder how on earth I can get home...

17:53.110 --> 17:53.820
Ah!

17:59.200 --> 18:00.200
Excuse me.

18:00.990 --> 18:03.450
A way to get back to your world?

18:03.580 --> 18:08.330
Sorry, but we're not in a fit state
to deal with that question at the moment.

18:09.540 --> 18:11.040
Right, Mock Turtle?

18:11.130 --> 18:16.090
Yeah, Gryphon and I have
got big problems of our own.

18:17.380 --> 18:18.970
Problems?

18:19.300 --> 18:22.100
Yes, I have a chronic heart disease.

18:22.550 --> 18:25.970
And I had faintly hoped that
the man I was with wouldn't be,

18:26.060 --> 18:29.350
but just as I expected,

18:29.480 --> 18:32.020
he turned out to be a spineless loser.

18:32.150 --> 18:33.020
A loser?

18:33.150 --> 18:38.320
I wasn't particularly hoping that he'd be like
a Sutherland and drag me along with him but...

18:38.450 --> 18:40.570
That would be oppressive in its own way.

18:40.820 --> 18:45.620
But, all he says everyday is
"Okay." and "Yes." and "It's up to you."

18:45.990 --> 18:49.330
You try and get by just continually hearing
those three expressions.

18:49.410 --> 18:55.340
I'm attacked by a combined wave of
anger I can't vent, irritation and despondency.

18:55.460 --> 18:56.880
Is that so?

18:57.130 --> 19:01.260
Well, you're still too young
to understand these things properly.

19:01.340 --> 19:05.260
Well... Take care of yourselves,
the both of you...

19:05.510 --> 19:06.390
Thanks.

19:07.980 --> 19:09.230
I'm jealous of her.

19:09.350 --> 19:14.150
There was a time when I was once
young and cute like she is.

19:14.230 --> 19:17.480
I really wish you could stop time...

19:17.570 --> 19:19.990
There's no way you can stop it, hahaha!

19:20.070 --> 19:21.860
Oh, my heart's stopped...

19:24.530 --> 19:26.580
Even though I'm still a child,

19:26.700 --> 19:31.580
when I grow up...
if I become a fine lady like my mother,

19:31.710 --> 19:36.040
I wonder if a wonderful
husband will come my way...

19:36.130 --> 19:39.590
First you need to get rid of
that overly doting brother,

19:39.720 --> 19:41.630
otherwise even insects won't be interested in you.

19:41.720 --> 19:42.970
Who are you?

19:44.340 --> 19:45.850
I'm the Cheshire Cat.

19:46.560 --> 19:50.100
Alternatively, how about
you living in this world forever?

19:50.560 --> 19:55.610
If you did, then that boy with his never satisfied
desire to control his sister wouldn't interfere.

19:56.650 --> 19:58.400
No, I'm going home.

19:58.530 --> 20:02.700
After all, if a guy better than
my brother doesn't come along,

20:02.780 --> 20:05.110
I simply won't get married.

20:05.410 --> 20:09.120
Hm, I guess with a brother who spends every day
of the year dreaming of his beloved sibling,

20:09.240 --> 20:10.910
you get a sister like this...

20:11.000 --> 20:12.290
Anyway, it's all good.

20:12.920 --> 20:16.380
If you go a little way from here,
you'll find the King of Heart's castle.

20:16.840 --> 20:20.250
You should aim for the forest past the castle.

20:20.380 --> 20:22.630
There should be someone there
waiting to show you the way.

20:23.220 --> 20:24.970
That's unforgivable, Nunnally!

20:25.090 --> 20:27.300
Thinking of things like weddings...
becoming a bride!

20:27.430 --> 20:30.220
I'll show you that I'm going to
look after you for the rest of your life!

20:30.390 --> 20:33.520
And as for that C.C., sticking her nose in...

20:34.270 --> 20:36.980
After receiving the Cheshire Cat's advice,

20:37.110 --> 20:40.270
the girl set off towards the King of Heart's castle.

20:40.690 --> 20:45.360
On the way she came across
a lion and a unicorn fighting in the town,

20:45.450 --> 20:47.780
but she paid them no attention.

20:48.030 --> 20:51.200
She just walked and walked intently

20:51.290 --> 20:55.500
until finally she arrived at
her destination, the castle.

20:56.420 --> 20:58.460
So this is the King of Heart's castle...

20:58.590 --> 21:00.250
It's so big.

21:00.340 --> 21:02.630
Which is the way to the forest?

21:06.180 --> 21:08.590
Girl!

21:08.930 --> 21:11.060
What do you want?

21:11.560 --> 21:13.560
Are you the King of Heart?

21:13.640 --> 21:15.390
Indeed.

21:15.520 --> 21:18.400
I want to go to the forest past this castle...

21:18.690 --> 21:22.020
You're saying that you want to go through the castle.

21:22.150 --> 21:23.030
Is it possible?

21:23.280 --> 21:25.280
Permission denied!

21:25.400 --> 21:27.950
But if I have to take a route around the castle,

21:28.030 --> 21:29.990
won't it take a really long time?

21:30.080 --> 21:31.490
Really!

21:32.450 --> 21:35.160
Why do you say such mean things?

21:35.460 --> 21:36.500
Your head,

21:37.830 --> 21:39.500
I'll have it chopped off!

21:39.880 --> 21:41.670
I'm sorry!

21:41.750 --> 21:43.550
Are you the Queen of Heart by any chance?

21:43.670 --> 21:45.010
I'm sorry,

21:45.130 --> 21:48.470
my husband can be a little thickheaded.

21:48.550 --> 21:50.140
So you will let me pass through?

21:50.220 --> 21:51.180
Yes.

21:51.310 --> 21:53.850
But on one condition.

21:53.970 --> 21:55.020
A condition?

21:55.100 --> 21:59.150
You have to play me at croquet,
if you win, I'll let you pass through.

21:59.230 --> 22:00.980
And...if I lose?

22:01.190 --> 22:02.270
Your head,

22:04.900 --> 22:06.860
will be chopped off! Ha-ha!

22:07.200 --> 22:08.700
That's not fair!

22:09.780 --> 22:10.990
Hold on a minute!

22:11.070 --> 22:12.740
That voice!

22:12.950 --> 22:14.870
It's the White Queen.

22:14.950 --> 22:17.330
I will play in this match.

22:17.410 --> 22:20.250
What?! What do you think
you're doing, White Queen?

22:20.540 --> 22:24.880
White King, I want to change my image
of being a mild mannered queen.

22:24.960 --> 22:27.590
Are you making light of me,
implying I'm weak and feeble?

22:27.720 --> 22:29.050
Not at all!

22:29.180 --> 22:31.640
I have a dream I want to fulfill!

22:31.720 --> 22:32.430
A dream?

22:32.550 --> 22:38.270
To win this croquet match, and let all of the people
use these castle grounds freely to enjoy croquet.

22:38.390 --> 22:41.100
I want to set up
a "Special Administrated Zone of Croquet".

22:41.230 --> 22:44.070
A "Special Administrated Zone of Croquet"!

22:44.190 --> 22:48.780
What an outrageous idea,
letting everyone freely enjoy croquet!

22:48.900 --> 22:49.860
Are you serious?

22:49.950 --> 22:50.910
Yes!

22:51.030 --> 22:55.240
God didn't make people who were above croquet,
or people who were too lowly for croquet!

22:55.330 --> 22:56.120
Well in that case...

22:56.240 --> 22:56.910
Eh!

22:59.750 --> 23:02.750
It seems I should accept the challenge as well.

23:02.830 --> 23:04.290
You're right, sire.

23:04.460 --> 23:06.420
The Red King and the Red Queen!

23:06.510 --> 23:10.970
First, I think we should
review these different opinions.

23:11.090 --> 23:12.680
You're right, sire.

23:12.930 --> 23:16.600
The King of Heart claims that
croquet should only be for the nobility.

23:16.680 --> 23:18.770
Exactly.

23:18.890 --> 23:23.100
The White Queen calls for croquet
to be open to all the people.

23:23.190 --> 23:25.770
Surely that is the proper way
for croquet to be played!

23:25.900 --> 23:27.610
Well then, let me dare to suggest...

23:27.730 --> 23:31.610
With this Fort Damocles I will!
Ooops, I will rule the world through croquet!

23:31.700 --> 23:32.110
- Grrr!

23:32.110 --> 23:32.450
- Grrr!
- Eh!

23:32.530 --> 23:32.950
- Ridiculous!

23:32.950 --> 23:33.320
- Ridiculous!
- Meh!

23:33.450 --> 23:34.700
You're right, sire.

23:35.200 --> 23:36.620
That was lucky.

23:36.700 --> 23:40.790
Thanks to everyone getting
so involved in arguing about croquet,

23:40.870 --> 23:41.960
I was able to go through the castle--

23:42.080 --> 23:42.960
Welcome.

23:43.040 --> 23:43.710
Huh?

23:45.460 --> 23:47.460
You've done well to make it this far.

23:47.710 --> 23:51.220
Are you the one
who's going to show me the way home?

23:51.300 --> 23:52.340
That's right.

23:52.470 --> 23:54.840
Whatever place you want to go.

23:54.970 --> 23:55.850
Don't be fooled.

23:55.970 --> 23:56.470
Eh!

23:57.890 --> 24:01.480
That Red Knight is famous,
even among other knights, for being a playboy.

24:01.730 --> 24:05.400
Really, only hicks say things like that,
White Knight.

24:05.480 --> 24:07.150
You have a bad reputation as well.

24:07.230 --> 24:10.650
If my reputation goes down for
doing what's right, I don't need it.

24:10.780 --> 24:14.700
What's more, people who make those judgments
aren't needed in this world either.

24:14.820 --> 24:15.870
Um, ah...

24:15.990 --> 24:18.740
Hm...are you challenging me to a duel?

24:18.830 --> 24:20.660
If you're not afraid of dying.

24:20.750 --> 24:24.250
Don't act tough
just because there's a cute girl nearby!

24:25.790 --> 24:26.670
Hah!

24:27.210 --> 24:28.170
Chak!

24:28.710 --> 24:29.380
Guk!

24:29.500 --> 24:30.500
Swashh!

24:30.920 --> 24:31.880
Amazing...

24:32.010 --> 24:35.180
I've never seen a heroic fight like this before...

24:35.470 --> 24:37.340
As expected you're a fine fighter,

24:37.430 --> 24:38.890
White Knight...

24:39.010 --> 24:42.390
No wonder you were crowned Knight of Zero.

24:42.520 --> 24:44.690
And you really are the Three Night Playboy.

24:44.770 --> 24:46.440
Don't make up strange nicknames for me!

24:47.310 --> 24:48.230
Haah!

24:48.900 --> 24:49.690
Thup!

24:50.070 --> 24:52.190
Swashh! Guk!

24:52.530 --> 24:53.360
Vzzt!

24:54.110 --> 24:55.030
What?

24:58.870 --> 25:00.030
You've got to be joking!

25:00.120 --> 25:02.870
I didn't want to fight...with you.

25:05.000 --> 25:07.710
Waaaah!

25:07.790 --> 25:09.840
That's ridiculous!

25:11.510 --> 25:13.460
That was a futile fight...

25:13.720 --> 25:15.130
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

25:15.220 --> 25:18.180
I'll take you to your original world.

25:18.260 --> 25:19.930
Oh, Mr. White Knight...

25:20.060 --> 25:22.220
Please mount my trusty horse.

25:22.310 --> 25:23.220
Of course.

25:23.480 --> 25:25.270
Right, off we go then.

25:25.390 --> 25:26.730
Lancelot Albion! Take off!

25:26.850 --> 25:28.190
Ah, wait a minute.

25:31.150 --> 25:33.440
Goodbye, everyone.

25:34.610 --> 25:37.570
Goodbye, Wonderland...

25:41.910 --> 25:44.620
And just like that,
rescued by the White Knight,

25:44.750 --> 25:47.750
gently rocking on the back of the white stallion,

25:47.830 --> 25:51.840
Nunnally was able to make her way
safely back to her world.

25:52.090 --> 25:53.630
Wonderful, wonderful...

25:53.760 --> 25:55.340
What was so wonderful?!

25:55.420 --> 25:55.920
Eh?

25:56.050 --> 25:59.640
This was all your doing, right?!
Sending us all to Wonderland!

25:59.760 --> 26:01.890
How are all of you in this world?

26:01.970 --> 26:03.930
It was really awful!

26:04.020 --> 26:06.230
And only you not involved, being all high and
mighty watching over us. Unforgivable!

26:06.520 --> 26:09.600
That's right!
And there was no Mad Hatter was there...

26:09.730 --> 26:10.560
Precisely!

26:10.650 --> 26:12.110
W...Wait a second!

26:12.230 --> 26:14.190
No way, there's no escape!

26:14.280 --> 26:16.150
Don't pretend you don't want to.

26:16.280 --> 26:19.150
It's perfect casting for you!

26:19.280 --> 26:22.620
Waaah! Waaah!

26:27.910 --> 26:29.960
Hahahahahahahaha!

26:30.420 --> 26:32.960
The Mad Hatter of Wonderland commands!

26:33.090 --> 26:37.340
All of you to come to my tea party and
make it the best ever!

26:40.300 --> 26:43.930
Who got butter on the Hadron cannon?

26:44.640 --> 26:49.140
Falling asleep in the middle of your story...

26:49.230 --> 26:51.270
Big brother, you really are hopeless.

26:51.350 --> 26:52.980
Right, Arthur?

26:53.320 --> 26:55.610
Meow!
